    {
      "key": "morris_useful_or_beautiful",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "Have nothing in your houses that you do not know to be useful, or believe to be beautiful.",
      "thought": "这句可以直接当首页文案的态度：实用或美，二者之外都不要。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Morris",
        "page_title": "William Morris, “The Beauty of Life” (1880)",
        "license": "quotation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "rams_less_but_better",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "Good design is as little design as possible. Less, but better – because it concentrates on the essential aspects, and the products are not burdened with non-essentials. Back to purity, back to simplicity.",
      "thought": "“少，但更好”——不是省事，是把不重要的拿掉。做首页时每加一个元素都用这句问一遍。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://www.vitsoe.com/us/about/good-design",
        "page_title": "Dieter Rams: ten principles for good design (Vitsœ)",
        "license": "quotation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "wabi_sabi_definition",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "In traditional Japanese aesthetics, wabi-sabi is a world view centered on the acceptance of transience and imperfection. The aesthetic is sometimes described as one of appreciating beauty that is \"imperfect, impermanent, and incomplete\" in nature.",
      "thought": "不完美、不恒久、不完整——这三个词可以直接当一组设计原则，尤其用来对抗那种过于光滑的 AI 感。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wabi-sabi",
        "page_title": "Wabi-sabi - Wikipedia",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "changwuzhi_ning_pu_wu_qiao",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "宁古无时，宁朴无巧，宁俭无俗。",
      "thought": "明代人的“反潮流”宣言。宁朴无巧——首页的动效和渐变都该按这句删。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/長物志",
        "page_title": "文震亨《长物志》",
        "license": "public domain"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "brutalism_definition",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "Brutalist buildings are characterised by minimalist constructions that showcase the bare building materials and structural elements over decorative design. The style commonly makes use of exposed, unpainted concrete or brick, angular geometric shapes and a predominantly monochrome colour palette.",
      "thought": "“展示材料本身而不是装饰”——网页里的对应物是什么？也许是不遮掩的排版结构和真实的照片，而不是插画。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brutalist_architecture",
        "page_title": "Brutalist architecture - Wikipedia",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "corporate_memphis",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "Corporate Memphis (also known as Alegria, big tech art, or flat art) is a term used, often disparagingly, to describe a flat, geometric art style widely used in illustrations of tech companies in the late 2010s and early 2020s. It is characterised by simplified human figures with disproportionate limbs and bright, often pastel, colours.",
      "thought": "反例。所有 SaaS 长得一样的原因。避开这个，也避开它的 AI 版本：蓝紫渐变 + 玻璃拟态 + 发光边框。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corporate_Memphis",
        "page_title": "Corporate Memphis - Wikipedia",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "liubai_definition",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "留白是中国艺术作品创作中常用的一种手法，指书画艺术创作中为使整个作品画面、章法更为协调精美而有意留下相应的空白，留有想象的空间。",
      "thought": "留白不是“空”，是让人有地方停。首页首屏想做成这样：一句话，一张材质图，其他都不放。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/留白",
        "page_title": "留白 - 维基百科",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "swiss_style_definition",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "The International Typographic Style, also known as the Swiss Style, emphasises cleanliness, readability, and objectivity. Hallmarks of the style are asymmetric layouts, use of a grid, sans-serif typefaces like Akzidenz-Grotesk, and flush left, ragged right text.",
      "thought": "网格 + 左对齐 + 无衬线，这套骨架永远不出错，但只用它会太冷。要和纸张、材质配着用。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Typographic_Style",
        "page_title": "International Typographic Style - Wikipedia",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "saint_exupery_nothing_to_remove",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "It seems that perfection is attained not when there is nothing more to add, but when there is nothing more to remove.",
      "thought": "文案的方向：不要说“强大”“革命性”，说我们拿掉了什么。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind,_Sand_and_Stars",
        "page_title": "Antoine de Saint-Exupéry, Terre des hommes (1939)",
        "license": "quotation"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "yuanye_wan_zi_tian_kai",
      "modality": "text",
      "content": "虽由人作，宛自天开。",
      "thought": "“虽由人作，宛自天开”——AI 产品最难的是这个：明明是机器做的，看起来却不像机器味。",
      "source": {
        "page_url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/園冶",
